In throwObject (src/engine.js), replace `recoilV: push.vA, recoilE: push.EA` with the dino's whole-body state after the follow-through has stopped the arm inside him. Momentum is P = pA - pArm. His energy E is torso plus arm, rest plus kinetic, because the arm's kinetic energy becomes heat inside him. Then v = P·c²/E, and the bulk kinetic energy is E - sqrt(E² - (Pc)²):

```js
let recoilV = 0, recoilE = 0;
if (!isFinite(push.pA)) {            // F = Infinity, footing finite: ultra-relativistic limit
  recoilV = K.c * obj.m / (obj.m + 2 * armMass);
  recoilE = Infinity;
} else {
  const pArm = push.pB * armMass / mB;   // the arm's forward momentum, returned to him
  const Pn = push.pA - pArm;
  if (Pn > 0) {
    const E = body.m * K.c * K.c + push.EA + push.EB * armMass / mB;
    const pc = Pn * K.c;
    recoilV = Pn * K.c * K.c / E;      // equals Pn/body.m when slow
    recoilE = pc * pc / (E + Math.sqrt((E - pc) * (E + pc)));  // equals Pn²/(2·body.m) when slow
  }
}
```

Return recoilV and recoilE from this block.
- If bolted: pA = 0 and pArm > 0, so Pn ≤ 0 and both stay 0 (the arm's momentum goes into the Earth).
- Real-muscle mode: the push values are finite and non-relativistic, so the formula reduces to Pn/body.m.

